On the average of both.

You can't completely avoid gaining levels, because then you get deep down
and the monsters are tough enough that they just kill you. There's no good
answer to the dilemma with Healers, but of course Healers are one of the
most difficult classes.

>	-  dive down to Sokoban ASAP, and get the goodies (hopefully an amulet 
>of reflection - I hate wands of death :P )

With Healers the "protection racket" actually makes some sense. Blitz for
Minetown while still XL1 (let the pet do the work) and donate for
intrinsic AC, then try and get out alive. After that I'd do Sokoban.

>Question #1:  at what point do you decide:  ok, I'm switching to 
>kill-everything-to-boost-my-XP?

I never explicitly seek to boost my XL (except if I'm waiting to go on the
Quest). It just happens. However, I'm happy to gain experience levels once
I have a good weapon, high Con and a decent armour class, becase then I
expect that an extra level boosts me more than the bad guys - I gain
plenty of HP, and I probably need skill slots for my main weapon or the
stack of daggers I am accumulating.

>Question #2:  at what point do you decide:  ok, I'm powerful enough to 
>go on my quest?

Depends on the Quest Nemesis. You can't do it until XL14; if your Nemesis
is a pushover (like Valks), you want to do it right away. If your Nemesis
requires special preparation, like the Cyclops (ie, the Healer Nemesis),
you obviously will want to wait until you are ready. If your Nemesis is a
hideous death machine, like Master Kaen (Monk), you may want to do it very
late, perhaps after cleaning out the Castle and using the wishes.

Have you ascended before? If not, don't start with Healers!
